Z||000013||fieroshop||08-25-2001||01:10 PM||||I have tested mine to see how they work. These hood vents are totally functionall at 10 mhp and at speeds of 125 mhp they help hold down the front end and there is no headlight doors popping open<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||G-Nasty||08-25-2001||09:41 PM||||Fieroshops hood vent kit needs minor reworking of the trunk seal. ALSO---I used the underside of some rear engine vents found on earlier fieros -they have that "honeycomb shaped holes" instead of the mesh Terry sold me. You will need to drive the car around after you glass and bodo it to fully cure it. Small cracks may appear after a week or two --make sure you fix them bbefore you paint it. Good Luck, You've got the best looking vents out there-||||reg||1
Z||000015||fieroshop||08-26-2001||01:46 PM||||G-Nasty, you are the first to have to do any mmodification to the trunk seal. These hood vents are designed to just install in the hood and not touch the weatherstrip. <BR><P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
